{"identifier":"Sniffles1955","title":"Sniffles and Sneezes","description":"Children as carriers and victims of infections.","videoUrl":"https://archive.org/download/Sniffles1955/Sniffles1955_512kb.mp4","thumbnailUrl":"https://archive.org/services/img/Sniffles1955","sourcePageUrl":"https://archive.org/details/Sniffles1955","durationMs":548001,"level":"B2","topic":"Health and hygiene","sourceCredit":"Source: Internet Archive — Sniffles and Sneezes","hasCaptions":true,"segments":[{"startMs":0,"endMs":31001,"text":"classical music Hey!"},{"startMs":32000,"endMs":33001,"text":"The symptoms are quite familiar."},{"startMs":34000,"endMs":36000,"text":"Very likely you'll come up with a correct diagnosis."},{"startMs":37000,"endMs":38001,"text":"Yes, it looks like a cold."},{"startMs":39000,"endMs":39001,"text":"A common cold."},{"startMs":41000,"endMs":44001,"text":"Runny nose, headache, achiness, very often a slight fever."},{"startMs":45000,"endMs":47001,"text":"Those are some of the symptoms of the common cold."},{"startMs":48001,"endMs":50001,"text":"Well, how do we get into that unhappy state?"},{"startMs":51000,"endMs":53000,"text":"Do we have colds, simply because of cold?"},{"startMs":54000,"endMs":56000,"text":"Because of ice, snow, and low temperature?"},{"startMs":56001,"endMs":57000,"text":"No!"},{"startMs":57000,"endMs":60001,"text":"Funny thing about colds, where is coldest?"},{"startMs":60001,"endMs":63000,"text":"The inhabitants hardly ever get colds."},{"startMs":63001,"endMs":70000,"text":"Explorers tell us that Eskimos are cold free, unless they come in contact with visitors from outside their frozen world."},{"startMs":72000,"endMs":77000,"text":"Then if it is not just cold weather, what is it that causes so many of us to catch cold?"},{"startMs":78001,"endMs":84001,"text":"Scientists think that most colds are caused by extremely small microorganisms, called viruses."},{"startMs":85001,"endMs":92000,"text":"Viruses, and there are many different kinds of them, can be scattered with each particle of saliva and mucus."},{"startMs":92001,"endMs":94001,"text":"When one sneezes or coughs, for instance."},{"startMs":95001,"endMs":101000,"text":"But do not think for a moment that cold producing viruses are spread only by sneezing and coughing."},{"startMs":102000,"endMs":112001,"text":"If by some magic, the tiny particles of saliva and mucus could be made visible as a black smudge, we quickly would realize in how many other ways we are apt to"},{"startMs":112001,"endMs":115001,"text":"scatter bacteria and viruses all around us."},{"startMs":116001,"endMs":119000,"text":"For instance, Jane here has a cold."},{"startMs":121000,"endMs":123000,"text":"Look at that smudge."},{"startMs":123001,"endMs":126000,"text":"Look at those germs she leaves on the doorknob."},{"startMs":126001,"endMs":128001,"text":"And here is Bob's hand picking them up."},{"startMs":129000,"endMs":135000,"text":"Bob, his hand now covered with germs, picked up from that doorknob, transfers them to a book."},{"startMs":135001,"endMs":146000,"text":"Sue, having the bad habit of wetting her finger to turn pages, carries the germs from the book to her mouth, and then passes them along with a pencil to Anne."},{"startMs":148001,"endMs":153001,"text":"Anne carries them home and leaves them on the family's dinner table."},{"startMs":155000,"endMs":163001,"text":"Yes, even during an ordinary conversation, saliva and mucus particles escape our mouth, and easily reach others who inhale them as they breathe."},{"startMs":164000,"endMs":167001,"text":"Just remember how breath becomes visible on a cold day."},{"startMs":168001,"endMs":173001,"text":"How then, with so many germs surrounding us, can we avoid having colds all the time?"},{"startMs":175000,"endMs":179000,"text":"Well, fortunately, our body has defenses against this enemy."},{"startMs":180000,"endMs":181001,"text":"Normally, we breathe through our nose."},{"startMs":182001,"endMs":190001,"text":"The nose, as well as the sinuses, the eustachian tubes, and the throat are lined with a delicate membrane."},{"startMs":190001,"endMs":200000,"text":"If, under a microscope, you look at the lining of the nose, we call it the nasal membrane, you can see that it is covered with tiny moving threads."},{"startMs":200001,"endMs":202000,"text":"These are called cilia."},{"startMs":202001,"endMs":207001,"text":"They move back and forth like stalks of grain when a wind blows over a field."},{"startMs":209000,"endMs":214001,"text":"The cilia are covered with a warm, moist, sticky substance called mucus."},{"startMs":215000,"endMs":220001,"text":"The nose usually secretes about a quart of this liquid every 24 hours."},{"startMs":222000,"endMs":227001,"text":"This mucus, by warming and moistening the air we breathe in, prepares it for our lungs."},{"startMs":228001,"endMs":234001,"text":"The mucus also catches and destroys microorganisms, that is, bacteria and viruses."},{"startMs":236001,"endMs":240001,"text":"The movement of the cilia carries the mucus down to the pharynx."},{"startMs":240001,"endMs":248001,"text":"Then it is coughed out or swallowed into the stomach, where any remaining microorganisms are destroyed by the digestive juices."},{"startMs":250000,"endMs":259001,"text":"If these defenses are weakened, the cold virus will gain a foothold and cause the inflammations, which so often are associated with the common cold."},{"startMs":261000,"endMs":268000,"text":"The common cold is not a serious sickness, but still, medical science as yet has not found a cure for it."},{"startMs":269000,"endMs":277001,"text":"Ah, yes, there are remedies galore, all sorts of medications, which soothe pain and headaches and so bring some relief."},{"startMs":278000,"endMs":281000,"text":"However, they do not cure colds."},{"startMs":281001,"endMs":287001,"text":"And no matter how convincingly they may be advertised, do not use them without having checked with your doctor."},{"startMs":289001,"endMs":292000,"text":"But there is a sound prescription."},{"startMs":292000,"endMs":300000,"text":"If you have a cold, don't stay in school, because if you do, you may send others home with your cold."},{"startMs":301000,"endMs":313000,"text":"If you have a cold, stay home."},{"startMs":315000,"endMs":316000,"text":"Stay in bed."},{"startMs":316001,"endMs":320001,"text":"This is the prescription which common sense and medical science recommend."},{"startMs":321001,"endMs":325000,"text":"Medicines, but only those your doctor prescribes."},{"startMs":325001,"endMs":326000,"text":"No others."},{"startMs":327000,"endMs":330001,"text":"Warmth, rest, which you can get best when you stay in bed."},{"startMs":331001,"endMs":334001,"text":"And while you're there, you might as well make the best of it."},{"startMs":348001,"endMs":351001,"text":"Right. Use tissues instead of handkerchief."},{"startMs":352001,"endMs":356001,"text":"That way you'll dispose of the germs much better than when you blow them into a handkerchief."},{"startMs":358000,"endMs":365001,"text":"However, should you not feel better in a couple of days, or if you keep on having a fever, you should ask your parents to call a doctor."},{"startMs":365001,"endMs":377001,"text":"You see, what you think is a simple cold could really be the first symptoms of some other disease, such as measles, infantile paralysis,"},{"startMs":378001,"endMs":387000,"text":"diphtheria, whooping cough, scarlet fever, influenza, and others."},{"startMs":390000,"endMs":396000,"text":"However, even if your illness proves to be only a simple cold, it is still important that you take care of it."},{"startMs":396001,"endMs":406000,"text":"A cold which is not treated might very well back up along the mucous membrane and so invade the sinuses, the cavities in the bones of the face and the skull."},{"startMs":407000,"endMs":414000,"text":"Or the infection may reach the middle ears when it invades the eustachian tubes, which connect the middle ears with the throat."},{"startMs":415000,"endMs":423001,"text":"Frequently, the inflammation also travels down the respiratory tract to the pharynx, the larynx, and the trachea."},{"startMs":424000,"endMs":430001,"text":"Your throat feels sore and your voice is husky. It travels to the bronchi. You have a bad cough."},{"startMs":432000,"endMs":435001,"text":"And occasionally even to the lungs, and that is pneumonia."},{"startMs":436001,"endMs":441001,"text":"These are painful complications and they often take a long time to clear up."},{"startMs":441001,"endMs":448001,"text":"The best defense against the common cold and all these other diseases is to keep up the body's natural resistance."},{"startMs":449001,"endMs":460000,"text":"To do so, you must eat regularly and well-balanced meals, that is meat, vegetables, fruit, milk, and so on."},{"startMs":461000,"endMs":465001,"text":"Get lots of exercise and fresh air, but do not exhaust yourself."},{"startMs":466000,"endMs":472000,"text":"In cold weather, you must wear sensible clothing to provide proper warmth to remain healthy."},{"startMs":475000,"endMs":483000,"text":"Go to bed at a reasonable hour. While you grow, you need about ten hours of sleep each night."},{"startMs":484001,"endMs":486000,"text":"Sleep recharges the body's energies."},{"startMs":487001,"endMs":489001,"text":"Protect yourself against infection."},{"startMs":491000,"endMs":493001,"text":"Keep pencils and other things out of your mouth."},{"startMs":495001,"endMs":497001,"text":"Never take bites of other people's food."},{"startMs":499001,"endMs":505001,"text":"Do not use somebody else's drinking straw or glass, not even within your own family."},{"startMs":506001,"endMs":510000,"text":"In the bathroom, for instance, use only your glass."},{"startMs":512000,"endMs":516001,"text":"And wash your hands frequently and thoroughly, especially before eating."},{"startMs":517001,"endMs":523001,"text":"When you wash your hands, you wash away many of the disease-carrying smudges you may have picked up."},{"startMs":525000,"endMs":531000,"text":"But if in spite of all these precautions, you still come down with a cold, let us repeat."},{"startMs":532000,"endMs":536000,"text":"Take it to bed and stay there until it has run its course."},{"startMs":536001,"endMs":548001,"text":"This is the safest way to regain your health and to return as quickly as possible to work, to fun, and to play."}]}